Pre-existing shared blocker resolved (required to unbreak the full-solution build/test for ALL prompts on
this integration branch -- same class of fix the 0010-ToolCard log documents):
  - TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj at HEAD was XML-invalid: THREE </Project> end tags (lines 968-970), failing
    XML load with MSB4025 ("Unexpected end tag"). Removed the 2 stray </Project> tags, restoring the single
    canonical Project root the file's own INVARIANT header mandates.
  - The same file also carried 20 duplicate <Compile Include> items (AccordionSection.Model.cs through
    AiUsageCard.ViewModel.cs, re-injected at lines 466-486), failing the build with NETSDK1022 ("Duplicate
    'Compile' items"). De-duplicated by keeping each Include's first occurrence (816 -> 796 Compile items,
    all unique). Both are classic .gitattributes merge=union concatenation artifacts; the repair is
    behavior-preserving and unblocks dotnet build/test/format.

