Web source: web/src/features/vehicles/components/vehicle-detail/QuickLinksSection.tsx -- a pure presentational
section (only data source is useTranslation; no data hooks, hence no loading/error/stale/offline branches,
exactly like the sibling QuickNav surface). Reproduced content states: Ready (the responsive tile grid) +
defensive Empty (the chevron-led "Quick Links" header always renders -> never a blank box).

Parity reproduced:
  - 6 tiles, in web order: Drives, Charging, Battery, Climate, Efficiency, Settings.
  - Routes -> W3 route names: Drives, Charging, BatteryHealth (path battery), ClimateControl (path climate),
    Efficiency, Settings (all present in RouteTable). Navigation via injected IQuickLinksNavigator (no HTTP in
    the view).
  - Segoe Fluent glyphs matching the destinations' RouteTable nav glyphs: \uE7C0 Route, \uE945 BatteryCharging,
    \uE83E Battery, \uE9CA Thermometer (web Climate; distinct from the Settings gear), \uE9D2 BarChart3,
    \uE713 Settings. Header chevron \uE76C (web ChevronRight), cyan accent token.
  - Responsive grid: grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-6 -> QuickLinksLayout.ColumnsForWidth = 2/3/6 at
    the Tailwind sm(640px)/lg(1024px) breakpoints; reflows on SizeChanged.
  - i18n (every string keyed; no hardcoded English): nav.drives, nav.charging, nav.battery, nav.climate,
    nav.efficiency, nav.settings, vehicles.detail.quickLinks (header/Narrator group), and the native defensive
    empty key vehicles.detail.quickLinks.noData. All resolve through the P1/S10 ILocalizer facade.
  - Accessibility: surface AutomationPeer is a Group named by the localized title; the grid carries the same
    name; each tile button exposes its label as the Narrator name; decorative glyphs are AccessibilityView.Raw.
    No custom motion (hover/focus is a plain colour swap), so reduced-motion is honoured by construction.
  - Telemetry: view.opened slug=QuickLinksSection on first Loaded; quick-links.activated slug=QuickLinksSection
    on tile activation (PII-safe -- never the route/label) per the P1/S11 diagnostics contract.

Deliverable gate (build + unit tests + format + placeholders) = all 0. The full-solution dotnet test is
non-zero solely because the WinAppDriver UI-automation runner is absent in this sandbox (see NOTE); on a
